   "source": [
    "Goal 1 (Design Evolution): Analyze how the visual design and structural complexity of major news websites homepages evolved over the last two decades.\n",
    "\n",
    "Goal 2 (Messaging Change): Trace how a specific organization's public messaging on a topic changed over time by analyzing press release text.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Define Dataset Scope\n",
    "\n",
    "Select 3–5 specific websites.\n",
    "\n",
    "Choose a clear time range.\n",
    "\n",
    "Plan to sample one capture per year per site.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Access & Collect Data\n",
    "\n",
    "Query the CDX API to get timestamps of all available captures.\n",
    "\n",
    "Fetch HTML content using:\n",
    "\n",
    "Direct URLs: https://web.archive.org/web/[TIMESTAMP]/[URL]\n",
    "\n",
    "Or use tools like Apify's Wayback Machine scrapers.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Analyze Data\n",
    "\n",
    "For Design Evolution:\n",
    "\n",
    "Measure page size, number of embedded resources.\n",
    "\n",
    "For Messaging Change:\n",
    "\n",
    "Perform text analysis: keyword frequency, sentiment, word choice.\n",
    "\n",
    "Always acknowledge limitations: incomplete captures, missing dynamic content, irregular crawl frequency, robots.txt exclusions.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Interpret & Narrate Findings\n",
    "\n",
    "Tell a story of change and the gaps in the record.\n",
    "\n",
    "Treat missing data and incomplete captures as meaningful findings about the fragility of the digital archive.\n",
    "\n",
    "Avoid overinterpreting causes.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
